@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Service";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] = "Terms of Service for SailScores.com sailing race results platform";
}
<div class="col col-lg-9">
<h1 class="h2">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<p>
    SailScores is a free, community-driven platform for hosting, publishing, and sharing sailing race results.
    These Terms of Service govern your use of the service. By accessing or using SailScores, you agree to be
    bound by these Terms. If you do not agree to these Terms, please do not use SailScores.
</p>

<section id="purpose-of-sailscores">
    <h3>1. Purpose of SailScores</h3>
    <p>
        SailScores is a community-driven platform for hosting, publishing, and sharing sailing race results.
        Clubs and individuals may use the service to enter scores, publish regatta information, upload
        race-related documents (such as Notices of Race or Sailing Instructions), and view results across
        devices.
    </p>
    <p>
        SailScores is not a general-purpose publishing platform. All use of the service must relate to
        sailing activities, race scoring, or club operations.
    </p>
    <p>By accessing or using SailScores, you agree to these Terms.</p>
</section>

<section id="your-account-and-responsibilities">
    <h3>2. Your Account and Responsibilities</h3>
    <p>You are responsible for:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>The accuracy of the information you publish.</li>
        <li>Maintaining the security of your account credentials.</li>
        <li>Ensuring that any content you upload is lawful and that you have the rights to publish it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You must not:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Misrepresent your identity or affiliation with a club.</li>
        <li>Create accounts or publish content on behalf of a club without authorization.</li>
        <li>Attempt to access accounts or private data belonging to others.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section id="acceptable-use">
    <h3>3. Acceptable Use</h3>
    <p>
        You agree to use SailScores only for lawful purposes and in ways that support the functioning
        and mission of the service.
    </p>
    <p>You may not use SailScores to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Upload or distribute illegal content.</li>
        <li>Upload malicious code, spam, or content intended to disrupt the service.</li>
        <li>Interfere with or overload the platform, including automated scraping or excessive polling.</li>
        <li>Publish content unrelated to sailing or club activities.</li>
        <li>Impersonate clubs, events, or individuals.</li>
        <li>Violate copyright, trademark, or other intellectual property rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Examples of prohibited misuse include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Publishing race results for a club without authorization.</li>
        <li>Uploading documents that infringe another organization's copyrighted Sailing Instructions or Notice of Race.</li>
        <li>Creating duplicate or misleading regatta pages to confuse competitors or clubs.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section id="content-ownership-and-license">
    <h3>4. Content Ownership and License</h3>
    <p>
        You retain ownership of the content you upload. By submitting content to SailScores, you grant
