    </p>
    <p>You represent and warrant that:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>You have the rights to publish any content you upload.</li>
        <li>Your content does not infringe the rights of others.</li>
        <li>SailScores does not claim ownership of your club's data or documents.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section id="our-right-to-remove-content">
    <h3>5. Our Right to Remove Content</h3>
    <p>SailScores may remove or disable access to content at our discretion if:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>It violates these Terms.</li>
        <li>It is unlawful or subject to a valid copyright or trademark complaint.</li>
        <li>It interferes with the operation or reliability of the service.</li>
        <li>It is clearly outside the scope of sailing-related use.</li>
        <li>It misrepresents a club, regatta, or organization.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Examples of situations where content may be removed:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Two clubs dispute ownership of a regatta name or initials; we may temporarily remove or hide
            the content until the dispute is resolved.</li>
        <li>A user uploads copyrighted documents without permission.</li>
        <li>A user publishes harmful or misleading documents under another club's identity.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We may notify you when content is removed, but we are not obligated to do so. You may contact us
        at <a href="mailto:info@sailscores.com">info@sailscores.com</a> if you believe a removal was made
        in error.
    </p>
</section>

<section id="copyright-and-trademark-complaints">
    <h3>6. Copyright and Trademark Complaints</h3>
    <p>
        If you believe content on SailScores infringes your copyright or trademark, you may submit a
        complaint to <a href="mailto:info@sailscores.com">info@sailscores.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>Your complaint should include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your name and contact information.</li>
        <li>A description of the copyrighted or trademarked material.</li>
        <li>A link to the content on SailScores.</li>
        <li>A statement that you believe the use is unauthorized.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Upon receiving a complaint, SailScores may:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Review the content.</li>
        <li>Remove or disable access if the claim appears valid.</li>
        <li>Notify the uploader.</li>
        <li>Allow the uploader to respond with an explanation or counter-notice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        SailScores will make a good-faith determination based on the information provided. We do not act
        as an arbitrator between clubs or organizations; our role is limited to maintaining lawful and
        appropriate content on the platform.
    </p>
</section>

<section id="disputes-between-clubs-or-organizations">
    <h3>7. Disputes Between Clubs or Organizations</h3>
    <p>SailScores does not adjudicate ownership of:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Club names</li>
        <li>Club initials</li>
        <li>Regatta names</li>
        <li>Logos or branding</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If a dispute arises:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>We may temporarily hide or remove the disputed content.</li>
        <li>We may request documentation or confirmation from the involved parties.</li>
        <li>We may decline to republish content until the parties resolve the matter independently.</li>
        <li>Our priority is maintaining clarity and preventing confusion for competitors and clubs.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section id="service-changes-and-availability">
    <h3>8. Service Changes and Availability</h3>
    <p>
        SailScores is provided as a free community service. We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any
